  "content": {
    "title": "Justin Bieber's Coachella setlist – Every song he performed in order",
    "text": "Updated April 12, 2026, 12:07 p.m. ETINDIO, Calif. − Justin Bieber made his comeback on April 11 at Coachella Valley Music and Arts Festival, riding on the vibes of his \"Swag\" era.The 90-minute set featured Bieber's mature side, showcasing selections from his recent two-part album, \"SWAG,\" including popular hits both recent and older.After the first 13 songs, something shifted in the vibe of the setlist. All of a sudden we stepped into the most laid-back retrospective arguably ever, with Bieber sitting on a stool in front of a laptop on a simple high table.He pulled up old music video after old music video, checking the livestream to see what people wanted to hear, and then he'd play a crowd favorite with the video displayed behind him while he sang along (or sometimes just jammed out without holding the microphone to his mouth).Honestly, it felt like you were in your childhood bedroom hanging out with a friend watching music videos, and it kind of ruled.Here's everything the millennial pop star played on Saturday, April 11:\"All I Can Take\"\"Speed Demon\"\"First Place\"\"Go Baby\"\"Butterflies\"\"Walking Away\"\"All The Way\"/\"405\"/\"Too Long\"/\"Petting Zoo\"/\"I Do\"\"Stay\" (with the Kid LAROI as guest)\"Things You Do\"\"Glory Voice Memo\"\"Zuma House\"\"Dotted Line\"\"Everything Hallelujah\"\"Baby\"\"Favorite Girl\"\"That Should Be Me\"\"Beauty and a Beat\"\"Never Say Never\"\"Confident\"\"All That Matters\"\"With You\" (Chris Brown cover)\"So Sick\" (Ne-Yo cover)\"Sorry\"\"Where Are U Now\"\"I'm The One\"\"Yukon\"\"Devotion\" (with Dijon as guest)\"I Think You're Special\" (with Tems as guest)\"Essence\" (Wizkid cover with Wizkid and Tems as guests)\"Daisies\" (with Mk.gee as guest)",
